rsisa berdasarkan ranking/EDAS yang sudah ada\"\\n\\n    This suggests that we have the EDAS ranking (the full list) available. But in the current frontend, we only have the playlist (which is the top N from EDAS).\\n\\n    We have two options:\\n      a) Change the backend to send the full candidate list (or at least a list of candidates beyond the playlist) to the frontend for the result page.\\n      b) Alternatively, we can use the current playlist and the removed songs to adjust, but then we don\\'t have other candidates.\\n\\n    Since the problem says \"jangan ubah flow EDAS utama\", we cannot change the backend to send more data? But note: the problem does not explicitly forbid changing the backend, but it says not to change the main EDAS flow, NLG, history, etc.\\n\\n    However, the problem says: \"Perlakukan ini sebagai modifikasi dari hasil/session yang sedang aktif, bukan generate hasil baru dari nol.\"\\n\\n    This implies we are only working with the current session\\'s result (the playlist we have) and we are allowed to modify it by replacing some songs.\\n\\n    But then, where do we get replacement songs? The problem says: \"mencari pengganti dari kandidat yang tersisa\". If we don\\'t have the candidate list, we cannot do this.\\n\\n    Let me check the existing code: we have the playlist in `result.playlist`. We don\\'t have the candidate list.\\n\\n    We must therefore assume that we have access to the candidate list? Or perhaps we can use the history? But the history is past sessions.\\n\\n    Alternatively, note that the problem says: \"lagu lain tetap dipertahankan kecuali penyesuaian urutan setelah hasil akhir dirapikan\". This implies we are only reordering the current playlist? But then we are removing songs and then we have to put back the same number of songs? But we don\\'t have extra songs.\\n\\n    Wait, the problem says: \"Pengganti boleh berupa satu lagu atau kombinasi beberapa lagu jika itu lebih cocok.\" meaning we are replacing the removed songs with one or more songs from the candidate set.\\n\\n    Since we don\\'t have the candidate set in the frontend, we must either:\\n      - Request the candidate set from the backend (which we haven\\'t done) OR\\n      - Use the current playlist and the removed songs to create a gap and then try to fill the gap by duplicating or using other songs? But that doesn\\'t make sense.\\n\\n    Let me look at the backend to see what we have. We are in the frontend, but we can check the backend for the endpoint that gives the recommendations.\\n\\n    However, the problem says: \"Jangan ubah flow EDAS utama, NLG, history, export platform eksternal, tema, atau area lain.\"\\n\\n    We are allowed to change the frontend and possibly the backend for this specific feature? But note: the problem says \"modifikasi dari hasil/session yang sedang aktif\", meaning we are working on the existing result.\\n\\n    Given the ambiguity, I think we must assume that we have the candidate list available in the frontend. How? Perhaps we stored it in localStorage? Or we can get it from the same place we got the playlist?\\n\\n    Looking at the code, we get the result from localStorage (RESULT_STORAGE_KEY). We don\\'t see where the candidate list is stored.\\n\\n    Alternatively, we can change the backend to store the candidate list in the result? But the problem says not to change the main EDAS flow. However, storing the candidate list in the result might be acceptable because it\\'s just for the frontend to use for this feature.\\n\\n    But note: the problem says \"bukan generate hasil baru dari nol\", meaning we are not recalculating the entire playlist from scratch. We are only adjusting the existing playlist.\\n\\n    Given the time, I propose a simpler approach that might be acceptable for the scope:\\n\\n      We will allow the user to select songs to remove. Then, we will remove them and then we will try to fill the gap by duplicating the remaining songs? But that doesn\\'t make sense.\\n\\n    Alternatively, we can use the same EDAS ranking but we don\\'t have it.\\n\\n    Let me think: maybe we can use the history? But the history is past sessions.\\n\\n    Another idea: the problem says \"mencari pengganti dari kandidat yang tersisa berdasarkan ranking/EDAS yang sudah ada\". We already have the EDAS ranking in the backend that generated the playlist. We don\\'t have it in the frontend, but we can make a new request to the backend to get the candidate list? But note: the backend might have already computed the EDAS and we don\\'t want to recompute.\\n\\n    We can store the candidate list in the result when we generate it? Then we can use it in the frontend.\\n\\n    Since the problem does not explicitly forbid changing the backend for this feature (it only says not to change the main EDAS flow, meaning the algorithm), I think we can adjust the backend to also send the candidate list (or at least a list of candidates beyond the top N) to the frontend and store it in localStorage along with the result.\\n\\n    However, the problem says: \"Implementasikan fitur ganti lagu di halaman hasil\". We are allowed to change the frontend and possibly the backend for this feature? But note the restriction: \"Jangan ubah flow EDAS utama, NLG, history, export platform eksternal, tema, atau area lain.\"\\n\\n    Changing the backend to store the candidate list in the result does not change the EDAS flow, it just changes what we store.\\n\\n    Let\\'s do:\\n\\n      Backend: when generating the playlist, we also store the candidate list (the full EDAS ranking) in the result that we save to localStorage.\\n\\n    But note: the problem says \"hasil/session yang sedang aktif\", meaning we are only concerned with the current session. We can store the candidate list in the same localStorage key.\\n\\n    We will change the backend to return the candidate list along with the playlist? Then we store it in localStorage.\\n\\n    However, the pro