{"time": "2026-05-17 12:15:31.439905+07:00", "level": "INFO", "message": "TRACE api.request.received", "module": "core.trace", "function": "trace_event", "line": 60, "request_id": "req_67d7b63c9e2c", "http_method": "POST", "http_path": "/v1/messages", "stage": "ingress", "event": "api.request.received", "source": "api", "message_count": 9, "snapshot": {"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 \u2192 4.6, 4.6 \u2192 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch\n</system-reminder>"}, {"type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder>\nThe user selected the lines 29 to 29 from c:\\Users\\Haikal\\Documents\\SKRIPSI\\GANTI JUDUL\\KODINGNYA\\frontend\\.env.local:\n1//05EH3dKOIoiyyCgYIARAAGAUSNwF-L9Ir7517_VOmNnNwwCZERczgaGFg94CnrpHbzr4YOYI8tjB3s8tXm2YGJOCquerpVdHIcAc\n\nThis may or may not be related to the current task.\n</system-reminder>\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-05-17.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "tes?"}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Our task? Let's see the last user message: just \"tes?\" It looks like the user typed \"tes?\" but perhaps they meant to ask something else? Could be a typo. Might be they are testing. We need to respond appropriately, perhaps asking for clarification. However the system information includes some context about selected lines from .env.local, showing some sort of key or value. The user might be asking about that? The message \"tes?\" could be shorthand for \"test?\" Maybe they want to run a test? Let's ask for clarification.\n\nWe should respond in Indonesian, as per language instruction. We can ask: \"Anda ingin melakukan apa? Sepertinya pesan Anda tidak lengkap. Bisa jelaskan lebih detail?\" Let's do that.\n", "signature": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "Anda ingin melakukan apa? Pesan Anda terpotong atau kurang jelas. Bisa jelaskan lebih detail tentang apa yang Anda butuh bantuan? Misalnya, apakah Anda ingin menjalankan tes, memodifikasi kode, atau sesuatu yang lain?"}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "tidak saya cuma mau tes aja apakah modelnya berjalan atau tidak, anda model apa?", "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The user is asking to test if the model is running and what model I am. According to the system message, I am Claude Opus 4.7. I should respond in Indonesian. I'll answer that I am Claude Opus 4.7 and confirm I'm running. No need for tools. Just a simple response.\n", "signature": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "Saya adalah model Claude Opus 4.7, dan saya berjalan dengan baik. Ada yang bisa saya bantu?"}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Implementasikan fitur ganti lagu di halaman hasil dengan model batch, bukan realtime per klik. User harus bisa menandai beberapa lagu dulu untuk diganti, lalu sistem baru memproses semuanya saat tombol Ganti lagu terpilih ditekan. Hanya lagu yang dipilih user yang boleh dikeluarkan; lagu lain tetap dipertahankan kecuali penyesuaian urutan setelah hasil akhir dirapikan. Saat diproses, sistem harus mengecualikan lagu-lagu yang dibuang agar tidak muncul lagi pada proses penggantian berikutnya di session hasil yang sama, menghitung total durasi yang hilang, lalu mencari pengganti dari kandidat yang tersisa berdasarkan ranking/EDAS yang sudah ada sambil tetap mendekati target durasi playlist. Pengganti boleh berupa satu lagu atau kombinasi beberapa lagu jika itu lebih cocok. Jika tidak ada kombinasi ideal, pilih kandidat terdekat yang paling masuk akal tanpa melenceng jauh dari target durasi. Setelah proses selesai, playlist diperbarui sekali saja dalam satu batch, urutan dirapikan kembali, dan user tetap boleh melakukan batch penggantian lagi pada hasil yang sudah diperbarui. Perlakukan ini sebagai modifikasi dari hasil/session yang sedang aktif, bukan generate hasil baru dari nol. Jangan ubah flow EDAS utama, NLG, history, export platform eksternal, tema, atau area lain.", "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Okay, the user wants me to implement a batch song replacement feature in the results page. Let me break down the requirements carefully.\n\nFirst, the key points from the user's request:\n- Instead of real-time replacement per click, users should be able to mark multiple songs for replacement first\n- Then process all selected songs at once when they press the \"Replace selected songs\" button\n- Only the selected songs should be removed; other songs remain (except for reordering after processing)\n- During processing:\n  * Remove the selected songs (so they don't appear in the replacement process again in the same session)\n  * Calculate total duration loss from removed songs\n  * Find replacements from remaining candidates using existing EDAS/ranking while trying to hit target duration\n  * Replacement can be single song or combination if better fit\n  * If no ideal combination, pick closest reasonable candidate without deviating too much from target\n- After processing: update playlist once in batch, reorder, and allow another batch replacement on updated results\n- This should modify the active session/results, not generate new results from scratch\n- Don't change main EDAS flow, NLG, history, export, theme, or other areas\n\nNow I need to understand the current codebase to see where to implement this. Let me first explore the project structure.\n\n", "signature": ""}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-99d024b4d66b0b81", "name": "Glob", "input": {"pattern": "**"}}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99d024b4d66b0b81", "content": "backend\\.venv\\pyvenv.cfg\nbackend\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\nbackend\\.venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\__init__.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\__main__.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\__pip-runner__.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\py.typed\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\__init__.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\build_env.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cache.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\configuration.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\exceptions.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\main.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\pyproject.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\self_outdated_check.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\wheel_builder.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cli\\__init__.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cli\\autocompletion.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cli\\base_command.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cli\\cmdoptions.py\nbackend\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\pip\\_internal\\cli